<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span><math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-Posteriors</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Approximate Reverse Marginals</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We parameterize the (generative) <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-reverse marginals to have a similar form as the true <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">posterior (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3 The Ψ-Posteriors ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)</span>. Therefore, the generative reverse marginals also factorize over the sequence length. Because <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#787878" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878">L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> is not available during sampling, there are two terms in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3 The Ψ-Posteriors ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) that are intractable. First, we choose to replace the posterior <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, as we cannot sample from <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{s}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{s}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math> without <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we replace <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>. Replacing these two intractable terms yields our generative reverse marginals:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi^{\theta}_{s|t}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=\kappa_{t}{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))+(1-\kappa_{t})\left[\alpha_{s}{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))+(1-\alpha_{s})\pi\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi^{\theta}_{s|t}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t})=\kappa_{t}{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}{q_{s|t}}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))+(1-\kappa_{t})\left[\alpha_{s}{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}=\mathbf{x}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))+(1-\alpha_{s})\pi\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that for the masked posterior (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1.1 Masked Diffusion Processes ‣ 2.1 Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ 2 Background ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{0|t}}(.|{\mathbf{z}}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t))={\mathbf{x}}_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof that the <math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-posteriors have the correct marginals</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi_{s|t}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{s|t}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}},{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-posteriors defined in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3 The Ψ-Posteriors ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> denote <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(k)=t(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(k)=t(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> denote <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. To prove that the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-posteriors have the correct marginals, we proceed by (downwards) induction, similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. (2022)</a></cite>. First, note that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{s}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{s}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as a marginalization over <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{s}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})=\sum_{\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}\Psi_{t}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})\Psi_{s|t}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell},{\mathbf{x}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{s}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})=\sum_{\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}\Psi_{t}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})\Psi_{s|t}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell},{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base Case</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{1}({\mathbf{z}}_{1}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{1}({\mathbf{z}}_{1}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the marginal at time <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3 The Ψ-Posteriors ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi_{1}({\mathbf{z}}_{1}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})=\text{Cat}(.|\bm{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{1}({\mathbf{z}}_{1}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})=\text{Cat}(.|\bm{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-posteriors have the correct marginal for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Induction hypothesis</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-posteriors have the correct marginal for a certain <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})={\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{t}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{t}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})={\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{t}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inductive step</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the induction hypothesis, we now show that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi_{s}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})={\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{s}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0B5396;" mathcolor="#0B5396">s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{s}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})={\color[rgb]{0.043,0.3242,0.5898}q_{s}}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(k)=t(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(k)=t(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{s}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{s}(.|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(1)}}{{=}}\sum_{\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}\Psi_{t}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})\Psi_{s|t}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell},{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#787878;" mathcolor="#787878" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(1)}}{{=}}\sum_{\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}}\Psi_{t}(\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}})\Psi_{s|t}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell}|\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell},{\mathbf{x}}^{\color[rgb]{0.4688,0.4688,0.4688}\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
