<figure id="A4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>FID on CIFAR-10 with ReMDM (best checkpoints, as shown in Table <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ D.3 Training Efficiency of Our Fast Curriculum ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental results ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). We sample with/without nucleus sampling, and with the 3 schedules of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025)</a></cite> (cap, loop, rescale). For the loop schedule, we use <math id="A4.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{on}}=0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{on}}=0.55</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{off}}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{off}}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{on}}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{on}}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, following ReMDM. Sampling experiments are executed in the original codebase of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
