<figure id="A4.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>
FID on CIFAR-10 with <math id="A4.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-samplers, where <math id="A4.T9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-samplers are activated for steps with <math id="A4.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{\text{off}},t_{\text{on}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>on</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{\text{off}},t_{\text{on}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A4.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is kept constant (according to the <math id="A4.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> column, <math id="A4.T9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise). We use the same checkpoints as in Table <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ D.3 Training Efficiency of Our Fast Curriculum ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental results ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Using a cosine sampling schedule and light noise injection (<math id="A4.T9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> close to 1) generally perform best. The CIFAR-10 curves in Fig. <a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ The Diffusion Duality, Chapter II: Ψ-Samplers and Efficient Curriculum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> show the best FID per number of steps.</figcaption>
