<figure id="A4.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Generative Perplexity (Gen. PPL) and Unigram Entropy on OpenWebText <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gokaslan and Cohen, 2019</a>)</cite> with ancestral sampling (no nucleus, no temperature scaling). We train using the log-linear noise scheduler, and sampling with the cosine scheduler is slightly better. We stick to the log-linear schedule for sampling in further experiments, to follow prior work, and since the cosine schedule only marginally reduces the Gen. PPL.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T12.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T12.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
